@hinthornw you are correct here, initially I was using older version of langgraph to debug that deep-agents issue. After version upgrade realized this already been fixed in latest version. 
**This is a LangChain issue**, not LangGraph

cc:@OiPunk

Hi! I'd like to work on this.

The root cause is clear — `to_openai_message_dict` puts `block.tool_kwargs` (a `dict` from Anthropic) directly into `function.arguments`, but the OpenAI Chat Completions API requires a JSON string there.

Fix in `llama_index/llms/openai/utils.py`:

```python
elif isinstance(block, ToolCallBlock):
    function_dict = {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
            "name": block.tool_name,
            "arguments": json.dumps(block.tool_kwargs) if isinstance(block.tool_kwargs, dict) else block.tool_kwargs,
        },
        "id": block.tool_call_id,
    }
```

Would a PR in this direction be welcome?

@Ju-usc, As @TomeHirata mentioned, reflection_minibatch_size is actually passed to gepa.optimize method, which instantiates a BatchSampler internally and that only selects reflection_minibatch_size number of examples.

Specifically, the make_reflective_dataset method will receive only as many eval_batch.trajectories, as the reflection_minibatch_size. Could you confirm this behaviour with maybe printing the length of eval_batch.trajectories?

What may instead be happening is that if the trajectory is of length N, specifically for dspy.ReAct, GEPA could be taking all calls, of lengths (1, 2, 3, ..., N) made to the model, and that could be bloating up the context.

Hi Tome, I didn't manage to make it work by switching the model. I get errors about MIME type which makes sense to me considering that `gpt-4o-mini` doesn't support audio. I tried multiple things regardless:

1. Using DSPy with `gpt-4o-mini` instead
LiteLLM raised an exception by OpenAI about wrong MIME type

<img width="916" height="488" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9c4b327d-8db0-4ee3-9819-8018a3c50e61" />

2. Use OpenAI SDK and the Files API
OpenAI returned 400 with the following message:

> "Expected a file with an application/pdf MIME type, but got unsupported MIME type 'audio/x-wav'."

<img width="1560" height="185" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d50f8e43-7b40-45e6-9ffa-72e2427efd1c" />

3. Use OpenAI SDK and upload file as Base64
OpenAI returned 400 with the following message:

> "Invalid file data: 'messages[1].content[0].file.file_data'. Expected a base64-encoded data URL with an application/pdf MIME type (e.g. 'data:application/pdf;base64,SGVsbG8sIFdvcmxkIQ=='), but got unsupported MIME type 'audio/wav'."

<img width="1459" height="265" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/62862904-786d-4d75-ace7-3eafe3081b2d" />

This is the code I used for the OpenAI tests:
```python
import base64
from pathlib import Path

import openai


def transcribe_base64(client: openai.OpenAI, audio_path: Path) -> str:
    with open(audio_path, "rb") as f:
        data = f.read()

    base64_string = base64.b64encode(data).decode("utf-8")
    completion = client.chat.completions.create(
        model="gpt-4o-mini",
        messages=[
            {"role": "system", "content": "Transcribe the user's audio into text."},
            {
                "role": "user",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "file",
                        "file": {
                            "filename": "audio_test.wav",
                            "file_data": f"data:audio/wav;base64,{base64_string}",
                        },
                    }
                ],
            },
        ],
    )

    return completion.choices[0].message.content


def transcribe_file(client: openai.OpenAI, audio_path: Path) -> str:
    file = client.files.create(file=open(audio_path, "rb"), purpose="user_data")
    completion = client.chat.completions.create(
        model="gpt-4o-mini",
        messages=[
            {"role": "system", "content": "Transcribe the user's audio into text."},
            {
                "role": "user",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "file",
                        "file": {
                            "file_id": file.id,
                        },
                    }
                ],
            },
        ],
    )

    return completion.choices[0].message.content


if __name__ == "__main__":
    client = openai.OpenAI()
    audio_path = Path("audio.wav")
    transcrition = transcribe_file(client, audio_path)
    print(transcrition)

```

